course: dictionary
lesson: 6358
title: MP: a short word with many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: MP is an abbreviation, a short way of writing a longer phrase. In the UK and other parliamentary countries, MP stands for Member of Parliament: a person elected to make laws for an area. «People vote for an MP, a Member of Parliament, for their local area.» The words vote and local area are the clues. Ask yourself: what kind of person gets voted for by a local area?
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right, because MP has several. «The soldiers on patrol were Military Police, who keep order in the army.» Here the words soldiers and army point to Military Police. In a music book, mp means mezzo piano: play fairly quietly. In a camera ad, MP means megapixels.
explain: To check a meaning, put it in the sentence and read it again. «Ella wrote to her MP about the new park.» Try Member of Parliament: Ella wrote to the person who represents her area. That makes sense, so it is the right meaning. Try megapixel instead and the sentence stops making sense.
fact: MP is short for Member of Parliament, a person elected to make laws for an area.
fact: MPs is the plural, which means more than one MP.
fact: «Our local MP» means the MP who represents the area where you live.
fact: In music, «mp» means mezzo piano, which tells you to play fairly quietly.
fact: MP can also mean Military Police, megapixel, or part of the file name mp3 for sound files.
exercise: «People vote for an MP for their local area.» What does MP stand for? | *Mezzo piano | Megapixel | Military Police | Member of Parliament
exercise: Your music teacher writes mp above the notes. What should you play? | Fast and cheerful | Very loudly | Not at all | *Fairly quietly
exercise: «The soldiers on guard were Military Police, who keep order in the army.» In this sentence, what does MP mean? | *Military Police | Mezzo piano | Member of Parliament | Megapixel
test: «Whips try to make their party's MPs vote together.» What does MPs mean? | Megapixels | *Members of Parliament | Military soldiers | Mezzo pianos
test: Mia's new camera has 12 MP. What does MP mean here? | Mezzo piano | Military Police | *Megapixels | Member of Parliament
exam: «Ella wrote to her MP about the new park.» What is an MP in this sentence? | A sound file on a tablet | *A person elected to make laws for an area | A way of playing quietly in music | A soldier who acts as police
